[ganderse@adelphi.ua.oz.au (Geoff Andersen) writes:]
[] Which {dragon scale mail} is better? Are they the same? I have resistance
[] to fire, sleep, shock, cold, poison and (I think) disintegration. I have
[] been told that only gray dragon scale mail provides magic resistance ...

all (+0) dragon scale mails provide 9 AC points.  with the exception of
gray dragon scale mail, each provides resistance to the attack of that
dragon.  gray dragon scale mail conveniently provides magic resistance
(which has the side-effect of providing resistance to magic missiles
amongst other things).  you want magic protection (which you can also
obtain from a cloak).

[] Also do the items in the polypile change their curse/blessedness. eg if I
[] have a +5 longsword will it polymorph into, say, a +5 katana, or will it
[] be +0 or some random variation. Similarly, will an item remain cursed under
[] polymorph?

one of the techniques for "proper" polypiling is to separate your items
into three piles each consisting only of cursed, uncursed or blessed
items.  the blessed states are preserved under polymorph.  you may also
want to separate your weapons according to their enchantments since
these are preserved as well.  wands tend to preserve their charges and
so on ...

[] Is there any difference between a cursed/uncursed/blessed ring of conflict
[] or for that matter ring of regeneration? I know you can't take off a cursed
[] ring, but are the effects different?

no ...

[] Lastly, I have a bag of holding. Should I bless it? I didn't quite
[] understand the spoiler sheet on this part. I will almost certainly be
[] going after the Wiz, and since he curses items, should I bless it for
[] that reason?

well, sure, bless it for that reason since a cursed bag of holding
doesn't work well.  if you need to carry a bag and can afford to
shuffle your inventory some then you might prefer a sack.

